  "design_notes": [
    "OC-13 compares the RAW Kafka JSON exports of regular and v2 by (Group, timestamp) because regular never publishes source_event_id.",
    "Every (Group, timestamp) couple is unique: timestamps are strictly sequential, no simultaneous pair, unlike the OC-12 fixture.",
    "HSTREE_INITIAL_WINDOW_SIZE=100 with SHAP_BACKGROUND_SIZE=100 (fixed in compose): events 1..99 are warmup on both sides (no local score, shap_values null).",
    "Events 100..110 are computed on both sides; outliers at 105, 109, 110 keep a normal/outlier mix without changing the comparison logic.",
    "Regular and v2 consume the same dedicated HSTree topic with their own consumer groups, so offsets and per-message SHAP seeds (seed_for_message) are identical."
  ]
